wh40k-class-specialization-overseer-pressure-doctrine-name = Doctrine of Subjugation
wh40k-class-specialization-overseer-pressure-doctrine-description = Weakening and disrupting hostile NPCs only.

wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-01-name = Right to Suppress
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-01-description = Unlocks the pressure stance. In version one, effects require direct observation and affect hostile NPCs only.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-02-name = Weigh the Enemy
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-02-description = Examining a visible NPC shows current threat, armor condition, and active tactic when its AI exposes one.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-03-name = Expose Weakness
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-03-description = Marks a visible NPC as the formation's weak point, giving recipients a detailed marker and briefly weakening one defined defense.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-04-name = Vox Interference
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-04-description = A voice or signal pulse briefly increases a visible NPC's next attack spread or delay. Players and devices are unaffected.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-05-name = Doubt in the Ranks
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-05-description = A marked NPC selects a new target more slowly after losing the current one. It neither clears threat nor turns allies against each other.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-06-name = “Break Formation” Order
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-06-description = Makes visible hostile NPCs in a limited sector spread out and seek cover again. It cannot move them through walls or control players.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-07-name = Exposed Position
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-07-description = An NPC hit during Vox Interference remains marked for recipients a little longer after leaving direct sight.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-08-name = False Command
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-08-description = Creates a signal at a visible point that briefly consumes a nearby NPC's attention. It needs a clear signal path and fails against immune bosses.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-09-name = Break the Rhythm
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-09-description = Two consecutive allied hits on a marked NPC briefly delay its next action. The trigger has an internal cooldown.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-10-name = “Fall Back” Order
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-10-description = Makes a weakened visible NPC retreat toward available cover or stop if no path exists. It is not a stun.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-11-name = Communication Breakdown
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-11-description = A pressured NPC shares less target and position information with allied AI. Requires a separate safe group-AI interface.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-12-name = Strike the Nerves
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-12-description = Briefly slows a marked NPC under fire from current recipients. Repeated applications do not stack.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-13-name = Weak Link
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-13-description = When a marked NPC is wounded or has damaged armor, its defenses are less likely to stop the next prepared strike. Healthy targets take no extra damage.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-14-name = Cascade of Doubt
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-14-description = Eliminating a marked NPC briefly disrupts nearby visible hostile NPCs. This is an AI reaction, not damage or mass control.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-15-name = Weight of Command
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-15-description = Sustained pressure gradually reduces an NPC's detection range for noise and movement only; direct vision remains intact.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-16-name = Sever the Plan
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-16-description = Interrupts an NPC special action when the Overseer saw it begin and responds within a narrow window. Version one never applies it to players.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-17-name = Voice of Despair
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-17-description = Strengthens existing suppression in a sector ahead, making NPCs seek cover more often without preventing all actions.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-18-name = Fall from Authority
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-18-description = Eliminating a target under two different pressure debuffs extends one debuff on a nearby NPC without increasing its strength.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-19-name = Total Priority
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-19-description = Designates one strong NPC as the recipients' shared target, emphasizing its debuffs and forecasting its next tactic. It neither executes nor strips armor.
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-20-name = Voice of Suppression
wh40k-class-skill-overseer-pressure-doctrine-20-description = Final node: combines marks, vox interference, and AI pressure in one capped modifier. It affects eligible NPCs only, never controls players, and never stacks between Overseers.
